+- Browser-only readiness defect (shakedown finding): a real browser fails the acceptance
+  `beforeEach` with a `cy.then()` timeout waiting on the global `appHasStarted`. `js/app.js`
+  already sets `window.appHasStarted = true` in `init()`, but `index.html` ships no
+  `<script src="js/app.js">` tag, so the app never loads in a real browser. The happy-dom
+  harness (`features/support/world.js`) masks this by manually `window.eval`-ing `js/app.js`,
+  which is why the in-harness suite passed. Crew fix: add `<script src="js/app.js"></script>`
+  to `index.html` (end of body, after the `.todoapp` section). The pin is the `@contract`
+  scenario "The served page loads the application script" in `features/todomvc.feature`, on the
+  watchbill; it reads the page artifact and reddens now, independent of the harness, so the
+  browser-only defect has an in-harness red target.
 
